<title>FRANCE: Rhone-Poulenc Q2 net income up 20.2 pct.</title>
<headline>Rhone-Poulenc Q2 net income up 20.2 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months to June 30, 1997.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of French francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net income				     934  vs	     777</p>
<p>    Income before taxes			1,799  vs	   1,696</p>
<p>    Earnings per share (francs)	     2.83  vs	    2.41</p>
<p>    Operating income			   2,151  vs	   1,815</p>
<p>    Net sales				   23,435  vs	  22,152</p>
<p>    Interest expense			     482  vs	     455</p>
<p>Operating income breakdown</p>
<p>    -- pharmaceuticals			   935  vs	     775</p>
<p>    -- Animal and Plant health		 867  vs	     805</p>
<p>    -- Chemicals				   380  vs	     214</p>
<p>    -- Fibres and polymers		     148  vs	     122</p>
<p>    Net income first half		    1,608  vs	   1,410</p>
<p>NOTE -- Rhone-Poulenc said it was maintaining its forecast of a 20 percent increase in 1997 earnings per share, before exceptionals. It said earnings per share for the second quarter would have been up 40.5 percent if not for the Centeon impact.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
